\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar ends U.S. mixed,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk aids yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 22:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The dollar lost ground to the yen on Tuesday amid growing speculation that Japan would try to reverse its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall with another bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the U.S. unit firmed against the mark on lingering worries over Russia's political and financial woes, while it also drew brief support from a larger-than-expected shrinkage in the U.S. trade deficit in June. \par \par \uc2  The dollar at the close was lower at 144.88/98 yen, down from 145.70/80 at the open and 145.84/94 at Monday's close. It was higher at 1.8010/20 marks from 1.7980/90. \par \par \uc2  Traders said talk that Asian central banks had been selling U.S. Treasury securities, perhaps in a bid to raise cash for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , greased the dollar's one-yen drop along with more rhetoric from Japanese officials that warned of such an event. \par \par \uc2  "The curtailment of dollar/yen's upward momentum to some extent can be attributed to an increase in verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Japanese authorities," said Bob Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas Corp., who added: "over time, if it's not backed up, it'll have less and less of an impact." \par \par \uc2  Kiichi Miyazawa, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister, said Tokyo is always ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the yen. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara noted market perception that the yen had hit a bottom of 147 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen also lost ground, piercing a key support at 80.80 that invited more selling, triggered stops in dollar/yen above 145, and buoyed dollar/mark. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was little moved after the Federal Open Market Committee left U.S. short-term interest rates unchanged as expected. Traders also said Monday night's mea culpa from U.S. President Bill Clinton regarding an inappropriate affair with a former White House intern sparked no dollar reaction. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said dollar/mark may garner support as uncertainty over Russia's political scene unfolds. Some expected fireworks when the Duma meets later this week to tackle controversial anti-crisis measures put forth by the government. \par \par \uc2  However, ongoing talk that European central banks have quietly sold dollars for marks at higher levels to stabilise the pair before the launch of Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union next year should dictate a narrow range for a while, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar belongs above 1.80 marks, certainly, but coming into EMU they're going to try and control it," said a trader at a French bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar drew modest support after the government said the U.S. trade deficit narrowed to $14.15 billion in June from $15.54 in May, but an initial push higher was short-lived. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Canadian dollar continued to stumble, slumping to $1.5301 to the U.S. unit amid worries over the Russian crisis and the release of a slimmer-than-expected trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars above C$1.53 but had limited success in reversing the trend. \par \par \uc2  "It's as much a confidence issue as it is with Canadian fundamentals, which are still fairly supportive," said Lynch. \par \par \uc2  "What would help the Canadian dollar is for conditions abroad to stabilise and that's not something the Russian default and devaluation is going to encourage," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended higher at Canadian $1.5285/90, up from C$1.5275/80 at the open, while Australia's dollar firmed to $0.5953/58 from $0.5886/91. The greenback firmed to 1.5100/10 Swiss francs from 1.5078/88 and the British pound edged higher to $1.6162/72 from $1.6140/50. \par \par \uc2  ((-Al Yoon, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1672)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8i01117\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
