\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Mixed; Clinton Speech Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 04:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was virtually unchanged at midday in Tokyo Tuesday compared with its levels early in the session, amid lingering fears of yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and caution ahead of President Bill Clinton's televised speech slated to begin 0200 GMT. The dollar is slightly lower against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Traders said bargain hunting dollar buying pushed the dollar from the intraday low of Y145.35. \par \par \uc2  "There are a whole range of players who were wishing to buy the dollar at the low-Y145 level," said Takeshi Nakauchi, a dealer at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  But he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be capped at the high-Y145 level temporarily. Earlier comments by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials reminded the market the overnight remark by vice finance minister for international affairs Eisuke Sakakibara that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen when the time is right. \par \par \uc2  In addition, profit-taking selling of the mark for yen spilled over into the dollar/yen trade and supported the yen, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  The strength in the Nikkei stock average and the firm tone in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also lending support to the yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  But others expect some dollar-buying to emerge after heavy after Clinton's speech, where the president is expected to explain to the American people his testimony to a grand jury earlier in the day regarding his relationship with ex-White House intern Monica Lewinsky. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT (10:00 p.m. EDT), the dollar is trading at Y145.53, virtually flat from Y145.55 around 0030 GMT (8:30 p.m. EDT) and below Y145.90 in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at Y146.51 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DEM1.7904, lower than DEM1.7950 earlier in Tokyo and below DEM1.7940 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.8015 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0204GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8i06yyx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
