\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Dn Ys Yen; Asia Mkts, Clinton Speech Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 02:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A rebound in the Nikkei stock average and a string of yen-supportive comments from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials brought the dollar slightly lower in early Tokyo trading Tuesday compared with its levels late in New York Monday. The dollar is slightly higher against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Participants said they will closely watch the movements of the Nikkei average and other Asia financial markets, particularly Hong Kong's Hang Seng index, for the rest of the Asian day. Hong Kong's financial markets were closed Monday and haven't had a chance to react to Monday's news of Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation. The Nikkei average is 97.05 points higher at 14,891.71 at 0040 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Also ahead is Bill Clinton's televised speech at 0200 GMT. The president is expected to explain to the American people his testimony to a grand jury earlier in the day regarding his relationship with ex-White House intern Monica Lewinsky. \par \par \uc2  But the situation in Asia is likely to take precedence, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Today's focus will be Asia," said Takashi Okura, first vice president at First Chicago Corp. "It will take a little longer" for the Monica Lewinsky case to start seriously affecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he added. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will conduct yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary. Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the ministry's international finance bureau, added that the yen's excessive weakness is unwelcome. He also said that the devaluation of the ruble is not a major concern for Japan. \par \par \uc2  Around 0045 GMT (8:45 p.m. EDT), the dollar is trading at Y145.55, down from Y146.12 around 0001 GMT and below Y145.90 in New York late Monday. It was at Y146.51 late in Tokyo Monday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DEM1.7950, just up from DEM1.7945 earlier and above DEM1.7940 late Monday in New York. It was at DEM1.8015 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0049GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 0109GMT) \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8i06yrz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
