\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar climbs on Russian woes, Tokyo stock slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab   0323 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     146.50/60\tab \tab 146.74-145.90\par  USD/DEM     1.8115/18\tab \tab 1.8045-1.7964\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The dollar climbed against the \par \par \uc2  mark in late trade on Monday, with worries about Russia renewed \par \par \uc2  by reports by Russian news agencies that Russia declared a \par \par \uc2  90-day moratorium on repaying foreign credits, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's strength against the mark and heavy losses in \par \par \uc2  the Tokyo stock market also lifted dollar/yen rate up, although \par \par \uc2  it was checked below 147 yen due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns. \par \par \uc2  "There have always been lots of risks in the Russian situation, but such dangers are now apparently coming to the forefront," said a senior trader at a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Russian's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday issued a joint statement introducing drastic changes in monetary policies in a bid to stop the financial crisis, Russian news agencies said. \par \par \uc2  The statement also envisaged changing procedures for setting the rouble exchange rate, expanding the rouble corridor and restricting foreign investment in Russian rouble instruments, they said. \par \par \uc2  The government-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement said it could keep the value of rouble in the six to 9-range per dollar until the end of the year, compared with a little more than six to the dollar so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the action signalled that the government could no longer defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and virtually devalued it. \par \par \uc2  "There is an impression that the timing of the devaluation came out earlier than we had expected," said a dealer at a German bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "This kind of sense could keep weighing on the German mark and could help push the dollar up above 1.82 marks in the near term," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said mark selling could continue for a while, but dollar sales interest by German exporters and by some European central banks may slow the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  Dealers here said since the dollar rose above resistance of 1.8050 and 1.81 marks, it may head torwards 1.83 marks. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 1.8013/16 marks and 146.33/36 yen in New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar gained against the yen due to heavy losses in the Tokyo stock market. The Nikkei 225 average was down 2.18 percent or 329.27 points at 14,794.66. The average ended below 15,000 for the first time since June 17. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the extent of the dollar's rise against the yen was not as large as that of the Nikkei stock fall, primarily due to continued worries over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda said on Monday that the yen at 146 or 147 yen to the dollar was excessively low. He also said Japan would deal with the yen's weakness appropriately when necessary. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be looming since Japanese officials were becoming specific on the dollar/yen rate, but others doubted there would be such action. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Eisuke Sakakibara said on Friday he thought the yen hit a bottom at around 147 yen to the dollar, and that it was now in a rebound phase. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese monetary authorities will be put to test whether they will really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the dollar tops 147 yen again and reaches 148 yen," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they would also watch President Bill Clinton's testimony later on Monday to a grand jury investigation concerning the White House sex scandal. \par \par \uc2  Clinton was expected to admit to an "inappropriate relationship" with Monica Lewinsky, but to insist he did not tell anybody to lie, a source familiar with his preparations said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Since this has been somewhat factored into the market, the testimony may not have a big impact on the dollar, traders said. ((Tatsuo Ito, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8h036it\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
