\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Down Slightly But Off Intraday Lows \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 04:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar is slightly lower midday in Tokyo Monday compared with its levels early in the session but is off its lows, after the downside held firm after a test of support just below Y146.00. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also lower against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Interbank players joined forces with Japanese exporters to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen, pushing it to an intraday low of Y145.94 at 0102 GMT, but the dollar recovered most of those losses after Japanese investors jumped in to buy dollars at bargain levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But concern over the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to cap the dollar's upside side, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is a bit top heavy due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Those fears were heightened by comments from Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the International Bureau at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , who said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "We have been saying we will act in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets appropriately, as needed," Kuroda said, adding that the yen's weakness and the dollar's strength is excessive. Later, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara added that the ministry's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unchanged. \par \par \uc2  But having confirmed dollar support around Y145.80, market players will try to test the upside, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Now that the market has tested the downside, people might try the upside," said another dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT (10:00 p.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at Y146.15, down from Y146.23 an hour and a half earlier and below Y146.30 in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at Y144.93 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DEM1.7983, lower than DEM1.7893 earlier in Tokyo and below DEM1.8016 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7863 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 17-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0223GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8h06ysv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
