\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Dn Vs Yen, Mark On Position Adjustment \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 02:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar edged lower against the yen in early Tokyo trading Monday compared with its levels late in New York Friday, as U.S. funds sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for yen to adjust positions. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking related dollar selling against the Deutsche mark also pulled down the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and weighed on the dollar versus the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday the dollar shot up nearly two pfennigs, trading as high as DEM1.8057 - a level not seen since July 15 - on fears that Russia was about to devalue the ruble. The mark is treated as a proxy for the ruble largely because of the heavy loan exposure German banks have to the Russia economy. Russian President Boris Yeltsin later denied there would be any devaluation of the ruble, taking pressure off the mark. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, concern over the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen continues to linger in the market, holding the dollar back against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Underscoring the determination of Japanese monetary authorities to talk up the yen, Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the International Bureau at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "We have been saying we will act in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets appropriately, as needed," Kuroda said, adding that the yen's weakness and the dollar's strength is excessive. \par \par \uc2  But weakness in Japanese stocks and ongoing concerns over another bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil in Asia are supporting the dollar's downside, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei stock average is down 193.26 at 14,930.67 around 0045 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT (8:30 P.M. EDT), the dollar was trading at Y146.23, up from Y146.12 around 0001 GMT but below Y146.30 in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at Y144.93 late in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DEM1.7893, higher than DEM1.7975 earlier but below DEM1.8016 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7863 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 17-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0044GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8h06yj6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
