\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS-Mark/Swiss calm on Russia c.bank comments. \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 14:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Mark/yen at lows, market watching for signs of dlr/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  * Official says Russia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helping some of biggest banks by extending credits at market rates. \par \par \uc2  * Russia stock market rebounds, trade suspended as index rises 15 pct. \par \par \uc2  * Russia President Yeltsin earlier rules out rouble devaluation, says Russia ready to resist new wave of world financial crisis. Yeltsin calls on Duma lower house to return next week to pass bills as part of anti-crisis package. \par \par \uc2  * International financier Soros says late Thursday in New York has no short position in rouble and no intention of shorting it, says letter to Financial Times was intended to issue wake-up call to G7 governments. \par \par \uc2  * Russia, emerging markets, mark all fell Thursday after Soros called for 15-25 percent devaluation of rouble in letter to Financial Times. Russian stock, T-bill markets improve Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark/Swiss\tab      at 83.30/33 vs 83.36/39 centimes late Thursday. Swiss July producer/import prices stable vs June, yr/yr fall 1.5 pct.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF's Sakakibara says seeking chance for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost yen, says Friday's yen rise vs dlr affected by mark movement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark/yen\tab      at 80.87/90 two-week low, vs 81.16/19 late Europe Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * German economics minister Rexrodt says Asia, Eastern Europe turbulence won't impact German noticeably. Rexrodt takes part in discussion on current economic policy issues 1330 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark/drachma\tab      eases from Thurs 6-wk highs after Bank of Greece \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling dlrs for drachma Thurs. Greek \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says current mark/drachma level compatible with policy of combating inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark/drachma at 167.68/78 vs 168.80 Thursday high, 168.55/65 late Europe Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Swedish July jobless rises to above-forecast 8.0 pct. Mark/Swedish \tab  at week's low of 4.5280/10 vs 4.5480/510 Thurs. Mark/Norway      4.2535/55 vs 4.2580/600.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Carolyn Cohn, London newsroom +44 171 542 6320, uk.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .news@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e036eg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
