\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr subdued,Sakakibara adds to  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  menace. \b0\par\par\uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 13:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The dollar's tone against the yen was subdued at Europe's midsession on Friday, with fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen continuing to weigh heavily on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar's softness against the yen was also dampening mark/yen, pushing it to two-week lows during European trade. This in turn was bolstering the dollar against the mark though the range here was small. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was heightened by comments from Japanese vice finance minister Eisuke Sakakibara. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was looking for a chance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also saying he thought the yen had hit bottom around 147 per dollar and was now in a rebound phase. \par \par \uc2  "Although the market thinks dollar/yen is going back up in the longer term, there is a lot of wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  right now. Particularly since Sakakibara has now mentioned a specific level like '147'," said Mitsuru Sahara, a manager at Sanwa Bank's treasury and trading department. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was at 144.79/89, off an earlier low of 144.35 but down from 145.08/18 seen late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen tracked a similar path, struggling near its low of 80.94 yen and down from 81.16/19 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Some, however, were wary of reading too much into Sakakibara's words. \par \par \uc2  "The market's chasing shadows. Much of it is speculation and suspicion rather than hard fact," said Tim Fox, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. "The fact that the market is moving so much on this shows how persuadable it is amid the illiquid summer conditions." \par \par \uc2  Even if push comes to shove, there was doubt about how far the Bank of Japan could drive down the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "They're being moderately successful right now in pushing dollar/yen down without actually having to do anything," said Sean Shepley, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Credit Suisse First Boston. \par \par \uc2  "But in terms of how far they could move the market...it's hard to see dollar/yen moving down more than one or two big figures from here without (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by) the Federal Reserve," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark had calmed down after a rally to a one-month high on Thursday, sparked by speculation of a Russian rouble devaluation, and a subsequent pullback. \par \par \uc2  It moved in a session range of less than a pfennig and was at 1.7895/00, near the day's high, against 1.7852/55 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Russia's President Boris Yeltsin took pains to mollify markets on Friday, vowing Moscow would not devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and appealing to parliament to hold a special crisis session to pass bills that form a vital part of the government's austerity measures. \par \par \uc2  The market was still poised to jump either way on news about Russia's financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  "I do not see the situation in Russia improving much, and with the uncertainty in Asia, dollar/mark will get to 1.80 again early next week," said one trader at a Japanese bank, referring to Thursday's one-month high. \par \par \uc2  In the way of data, U.S. producer price inflation for July is due at 1230 GMT, with both the headline and core PPI expected to have risen by 0.1 percent. Headline prices dropped by 0.1 and core prices rose by 0.2 in June. \par \par \uc2  U.S. July industrial production, due at 1315 GMT, is forecast to have dropped 0.5 percent after a 0.6 percent fall previously. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e036d2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
