\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan dollar ends higher as yen rebounds. \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 10:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar closed higher on Friday as the Japanese yen rose to above 145 against the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar, which opened firmer at T$34.743, extended its gains to end at T$34.702 against Thursday's T$34.771 close. \par \par \uc2  Turnover through dealers was active at US$275 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the key factor was a rise in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which gained some two yen to the U.S. dollar on comments by finance vice minister Eisuke Sakakibara that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was looking for a chance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and boost the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used the rare opportunity of a rising Taiwan dollar to nudge the rate higher, moving quietly into the market to buy up the local unit. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  knows it cannot buck the trend, so it has taken advantage of the yen's rise to further boost the Taiwan dollar," said one dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that recently brisk U.S. dollar buying had been slowed by the bank's brisk Taiwan dollar defence. \par \par \uc2  "Buyers have become very cautious following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days. It's very obvious the bank will continue its defence," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Taiwan dollar would continue to mirror the yen's movements. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's second market, Cosmos \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which opened firmer at T$34.75, also firmed to end at T$34.710 against Thursday's T$34.785 close. It traded between T$34.710-763. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e0353j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
