\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr powers higher on Russia, Hang Seng worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 09:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0600 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     146.98/00\tab \tab 147.16-145.86\par  USD/DEM     1.7967/69\tab \tab 1.8002-1.7871\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against the \par \par \uc2  yen and the mark in late afternoon Tokyo on Thursday, propelled \par \par \uc2  by worries over Russia's financial situation and by sharp \par \par \uc2  losses in Hong Kong's stock market. \par \par \uc2  But the market was cautious about buying the greenback too \par \par \uc2  aggressively after a senior Japanese Finance Ministry official \par \par \uc2  hinted at a dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice finance minister for international affairs, said on Thursday he expected a turning point for Japan's economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August and September and that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was looking for chances to conduct yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped as low as 145.86 yen earlier on Thursday after Sakakibara's comments. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback moved higher in the afternoon following a sharp drop in Hong Kong stocks. The key Hang Seng index ended Thursday's morning session down 274.24 points or 4.0 percent at 6,585.24. \par \par \uc2  Dollar buying was led mainly by U.S. fund operators. \par \par \uc2  "The market was susceptible to large-lot buying and selling by overseas operators as many Japanese players are away for holidays this week," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  The greenback also powered ahead against the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rising as high as 1.8002 marks after stop-loss buying was triggered above 1.7950 marks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Lingering concerns that Russia may have to devalue the rouble weighed on the mark," said a dealer at another city bank. "More stop-loss dollar buying is expected above 1.80 marks." \par \par \uc2  Worries about Russia heightened after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it will impose emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits on its commercial banks from Thursday to bolster the battered rouble. \par \par \uc2  Fears about Russia's financial situations were also exacerbated by a report that international financier George Soros called for a devaluation of the rouble. \par \par \uc2  In a letter to the Financial Times, Soros also suggested the introduction of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegged to the dollar or euro. \par \par \uc2  Soros said Russia's financial markets had "reached a terminal phase", the paper said on its Thursday edition. \par \par \uc2  Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy chairman Denis Kiselyov said Soros's proposals would not solve Russia's financial crisis. He said Russia's existing \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy would help avoid a banking crisis. \par \par \uc2  The mark tends to be sold against the dollar and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever worries about the Russian economy surface, because of German banks' heavy exposure to Russia. \par \par \uc2  The market was unmoved by Japan's current account data for June. Japan's current account surplus rose 46.2 percent from a year earlier to 1.44 trillion yen in June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said fears that the yen's prolonged weakness could prompt central banks in other countries to reduce yen in their external reserves also were a factor that weighed on the yen on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trimming back the yen portion of the island's external reserves to ensure maximum returns, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  department chief Chou Ah-ting said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chou declined to specify to what extent the bank is reducing the yen, but said Taiwan's actions were in line with those of other central banks around the world. \par \par \uc2  The news about Taiwan followed a similar report about mainland China earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The Financial Times said on Tuesday that China has sharply reduced its yen-denominated reserve holdings to protect the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 146.15/25 yen and 1.7850/55 marks in New York on Wednesday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8d031fx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
