\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Profit-taking Cited In Dollar/Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 22:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, upward momentum in the dollar/yen slowed on some profit-taking, as market participants unwound short yen positions in the New York session, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar posted intraday highs in early trading on news that the U.S. may be reluctant to join in any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the yen's slide. \par \par \uc2  Still, fears linger, even if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only come from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, said Thursday: "August and September are a turning point for the Japanese economy. We are waiting for an opportunity for a (yen) supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Bank of Cananda \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, as the Canadian dollar slid against its U.S. counterpart Thursday. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at C$1.5200. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has been pressed by the uncertainty in Asia and Russia, as well as falling commodity prices. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets for six consecutive sessions. At 2020 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5190, down slightly from C$1.5204 late Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official Wednesday close for the U.S. dollar was C$1.5193. \par \par \uc2  But Russia remained the attention-grabber Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Russian stock market resumed its free-fall Thursday as the RTS index closed down 6.5% after trading was suspended earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  The Russian ruble ended lower against the dollar on spotty trading. The dollar for next-day delivery closed at RUR6.3775, up from RUR6.3150 at Wednesday's close. The ruble remained below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily lower trading limit of RUR6.2460 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  (For more detail on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, please see page 1033.) \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2042GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 28038 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8d06wbp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
