\par\par \b \uc2  Treasury confirms Rubin, Miyazawa to meet in Sept. \b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 16:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Aug 12 (Reuters) - Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin and Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa will meet in San Francisco early in September, a Treasury Department spokesman confirmed on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "As Finance Minister Miyazawa said yesterday, he and Secretary Rubin will be meeting the first weekend in September," the spokesman said. No specific date and time for the meeting has been set yet, he said. \par \par \uc2  The spokesman declined to comment on a possible agenda for the meeting between Rubin and Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, in Tokyo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told reporters the two will discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, the Japanese economy and issues concerning Russia and Asia. \par \par \uc2  The yen hit an eight-year low against the dollar on Tuesday of 147.35 but recovered to around 145.88 in Wednesday trading, partly on concerns that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the ministry was in close contact with U.S. authorities on recent developments in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and the dollar/yen exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  U.S. officials have refused any comment on exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  ((Washington newsroom, +1 202 898-8395, fax +1 202 898-8383, washington.economic.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8c02zf0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
