\par\par \b \uc2  Some Asian markets take respite as yen firms. \b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 08:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 12 (Reuters) - Some Asian financial markets took a respite on Wednesday as the yen regained ground amid growing caution over a possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stocks were down following an overnight drop in New York stocks, but pared losses by midday on the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei average index ended Wednesday's morning session down 56.29 points or 0.37 percent at 15,350.70, after falling as low as 15,269.83. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong stocks, which had plummeted to five-year lows on Tuesday, were higher in early trading on futures-related buying and a firmer yen. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng index was up 1.34 percent at 6,871.09, after briefly falling as low as 6,708.18 earlier as of 0313 GMT. \par \par \uc2  But bourses in South Korea and Taiwan were down following a drop in Wall Street stocks and lingering concerns over the yen. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's composite index was down 2.21 percent at 304.36 at midday break. Taiwan's benchmark stock index was down 0.86 percent at 7,320.14 at 0313 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mounted as the yen's Tuesday fall to an eight-year low of 147.64 yen to the dollar sent shock waves to financial markets worldwide, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly dipped as low as 145.40 yen on Wednesday, down about two yen from an earlier high of 147.43 yen, on a wave of stop-loss selling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar selling heated up also on comments from senior officials of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara told reporters on Tuesday there is no change in the Japanese government's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when it is deemed necessary. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of the ministry's International Bureau, said Japan is strongly concerned about the yen's recent weakness and is ready to take action on it as necessary in the future. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda also said an excessively weak yen which did not reflect economic fundamentals was undesirable not only for Japan but also for Asia and the rest of the world. \par \par \uc2  "The Dow's close off its low and the yen's recovery after Sakakibara comments kept the Nikkei average from diving sharply," said Masatoshi Sato, manager at Kankaku Securities. \par \par \uc2  New York's Dow Jones industrial ended down 112.00 points or 1.3 percent at 8,462.85 on Tuesday after briefly falling as much as 250 points. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 146.15/17 yen at midday in Tokyo, compared with 147.22/32 yen in New York late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "If the dollar returns above 147 yen and stays above that level too long, it would cause a lot of problems for Asia," said Yasuji Yamanaka, chief manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division at Nikko Trust and Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2  "So a concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is highly likely in the future. But a concerted action is likely come only after Japan's ruling party reaches compromise with the opposition on the banking bills," he added. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi, whose ruling Liberal Demorcratic Party does not have a majority in the Upper House of parliament, has said he is willing to compromise with the opposition on the key financial bills. \par \par \uc2  These bills are needed to set up a "bridge bank" scheme to wind up failed banks while providing loans to "healthy" borrowers. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ alone is possible before such a compromise is reached, but its impact would be small compared with a joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroomreuters.com)) (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8c02y3d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
