\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar upside remains heavy in mid-morning Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 04:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 12 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0151 GMT --*Dollar's upside remains heavy against yen by \par \par \uc2  mid-morning Tokyo on Wednesday amid profit-taking and continued \par \par \uc2  long-liquidation. *Greenback hovering near 146 yen after \par \par \uc2  earlier wave of stop-loss sales. \par \par \uc2      *Speculative players, Japanese exporters seek to sell on \par \par \uc2  rallies, with resistance seen near 146.40/70 yen. \par \par \uc2      *But downside steady on Japanese players looking to pick up \par \par \uc2  dollar, mark/yen on dips. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar at 146.15/25 yen versus 147.22/32 in late New York \par \par \uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  *Some Japanese importers picked up dollars. *Some dealers noted dollar-buying related to setting up of investment trusts. *Concerns over possible yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rising after comments by monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  *Following earlier remarks, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara said on Wednesday that Japan will adopt an aggressive stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and other policy issues, Jiji news agency reported. \par \par \uc2  *A dealer at a city bank said although Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone would have a limited impact, remarks by Sakakibara had made players less keen to chase the upside. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers also to keep eye on Tokyo stocks, especially bank stocks, and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equities. \par \par \uc2  *Benchmark Nikkei stock average ended morning session down 56.29 points at 15,350.70. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar could also tumble on further long-liquidation and technical sales. Stop-loss sales still remain in 146 yen range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  0030 GMT - *Dollar fell sharply against yen in early Tokyo on wave of stop-loss selling. \par \par \uc2  *Greenback briefly fell about two yen from earlier highs on selling, seen as profit-taking and speculative attempts to trigger stop-losses, led by U.S. and European fund operators. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar's fall abrupt, but dealers said no talk of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far. \par \par \uc2  *"The market had been cautious from earlier in the day about possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This morning's price moves were exaggerated by thin volume," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Some dealers said comments on Wednesday by senior Finance Ministry officials also encouraged dollar long liquidation. \par \par \uc2  *Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said there is no change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when deemed necessary. \par \par \uc2  *Haruhiko Kuroda, head of ministry's International Bureau, said Japan is strongly concerned about yen's recent weakness and is ready to take action on it as necessary in future. \par \par \uc2  *Number of market participants in Tokyo limited due to Japan's mid-August holiday period, dealers said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8c02xmz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
