\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese Think-Tanks: Devaluation Not Needed Despite Weak Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 07:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BEIJING (Dow Jones)--Chinese government think-tanks on Wednesday echoed a top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official's reaffirmation Tuesday that country doesn't need to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the weak yen, and that a yuan devaluation would do more harm than good. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan has no need to be devalued and should not be devalued," Zhao Yixin, a finance expert at Chinese Academy of Social Science's Economic Research Center, said in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  Even if the yen were to drop to Y150 against the dollar, China wouldn't have to devalue its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Zhao said. \par \par \uc2  Zhao wouldn't make any predictions on how far the yen would have to fall before the Chinese government reevaluates its yuan policy. \par \par \uc2  However, he said the yen isn't likely to depreciate much further than current levels, which are near where the U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late June to prop up the yen. \par \par \uc2  At 0506 GMT, the dollar was at Y146.78. \par \par \uc2  The yen dropped to an eight-year low against the dollar in Asian trading Tuesday, prompting a sell-off in regional equity markets and reviving fears of a yuan devaluation. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's slump has put tremendous pressure on China," Zhao said. "Japan, as a big economy, has the capability to stabilize its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it doesn't seem to be willing to do so." \par \par \uc2  As one of China's biggest export markets and a main foreign investor, Japan's lagging economy has hurt China's export growth and foreign investment flows. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 12-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0511GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8c06tq8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
