\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Kuroda "Unhappy" With Weak Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 08:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Also weighing on the yen were notions that Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi could have trouble seeing through the passage in parliament of key financial system bills. Opposition parties, in a bid to take advantage of Obuchi's lack of popularity with the public, have been trying to force Obuchi to dissolve parliament and call early elections. \par \par \uc2  The yen's plunge to new 8-year lows drew a fresh round of objections from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After the dollar broke above Y147.00, Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the ministry's International Bureau, told a small group of reporters, "I've said over and over again (recently) that I'm not happy about the excessively weak yen, so in this case I'm extremely unhappy about it." \par \par \uc2  That comment came after Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Vice Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara reminded the market earlier in the day that action by monetary authorities to support the yen is a real possibility. \par \par \uc2  Many traders expressed doubts that the U.S. would join such an effort. \par \par \uc2  "Unless China puts pressure on the U.S. government, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be coordinated," said Shuji Takano, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at ABN Amro Bank. \par \par \uc2  Any solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely would have little long-term impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yen's weakness against the Deutsche mark also is weighing on the yen versus the dollar, as the yen is dropping across the board against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at Y82.44, up from Y82.33 in New York late Monday and above Y82.38 in London late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6307, down from $1.6353 in New York late Monday. Sterling was at $1.6343 in London late Monday. Sterling is quoted at Y240.54, up from Y239.04 in New York late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By James Simms; 813-5255-2929; jsimms@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0637GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8b06tx4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
