\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Eases On MOF Comments But Well Supported \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 04:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen from senior officials at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  encouraged a mild round of dollar selling Tuesday, bringing it lower from its levels earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and vice minister for international affairs Eisuke Sakakibara reminded the market that action to support the yen remains a possibility as the dollar nears an eight-year high against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but market participants said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point wouldn't change the fundamental dollar-bullishness. \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market isn't moving in an orderly way, it could cause disruption in the market, and to prevent that, we won't hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Miyazawa said. That comment came minutes after Sakakibara expressed his "grave concerns" about the yen's weakness. \par \par \uc2  While the comments pulled the dollar from its intraday high of Y146.55 at 0009 GMT (8:09 p.m. EDT Monday), traders attributed the selling as much to a lack of momentum in a thin market as anything else. With much of Japan on its week-long "Obon" holidays, trading is muted. \par \par \uc2  "There is nobody trading except interbank dealers," said a Japanese bank trader. "There was some impact (from Miyazawa and Sakakibara), but not a whole lot. There just doesn't seem to be enough buying to kick the dollar past Y146.50." \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be a surprise with the dollar this strong, participants doubted that the rest of the Group of Seven countries would rush to help \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  defend the yen. Solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't expected to have a long-term impact, due to deepset doubts about the health of Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt that the U.S. is going to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  without more policy commitments from Tokyo to help the economy," a Japanese trust bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT, the dollar is trading at Y146.30, down from Y146.45 around 0030 GMT but above Y146.18 in New York late Monday. The dollar was at Y146.48 in Tokyo late Monday. It is also trading at DEM1.7800, flat from DEM1.7804 earlier in Tokyo but above DM1.7755 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.7806 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 11-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0202GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8b06t19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
