\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar idles at Europe midday ahead of major peak. \b0\par\par\uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 12:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The dollar ran out of steam at midsession on Monday as yen bears ceded ground to dollar profit-takers in sluggish European trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen firmed closer to this year's high at 146.75 as the yen took another beating amid concern about weak Tokyo stocks and speculation about a Chinese yuan devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers expect a slow grind higher toward the 150 yen level, with no end in sight to bearish news out of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The market was nervous ahead of the 146.75 peak, the dollar's highest level since August 1990. After the dollar hit this level in mid-June, the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sprang a surprise on the market by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's going to be a slow process to get to 150 because the risk is that if you chase the dollar higher that quickly you might get your fingers burnt if there's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Michael Wallace, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysis Europe at Standard and Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  At 1030 GMT the dollar traded at 146.45/55 yen and 1.7808/13 marks, compared with 146.25/35 and 1.7805/15 in late European trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen hovered around Friday's 5-1/2 year high at 82.31 yen, up from 82.13/15 at the close. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise was spurred in Asian trade by news that unlisted Japanese copier maker Mita Industrial Co Ltd announced it had filed for court protection from its creditors, with liabilities exceeding 200 billion yen ($1.36 billion). \par \par \uc2  The news increased worries about further insolvencies in Japan, hurting sentiment on Japanese stocks, with the Nikkei closing down 1.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said concern about Japan's slowness in fixing its banking system was weighing on the yen as the markets eagerly awaited news about the governments' bridge bank plan. \par \par \uc2  Signs that the programme will not be geared towards the largest banks or that it will put more emphasis on short-term life support measures than on speedy banking system regulation will put more pressure on the yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  A big hurdle facing the reform efforts of Japan's new government is the possibility of a rocky passage in the Diet for its banking sector reform bills as opposition Democrats have threatened to oppose the plan. \par \par \uc2  Speculation about a Chinese yuan devaluation and a possible de-linking of the Hong Kong and the U.S. dollars was likely to keep the dollar solid against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Chinese President Jiang Zemin reiterated on Sunday that Beijing was determined to avoid devaluaing the yuan despite a slowing economy. \par \par \uc2  "Despite no action to devalue the yuan over the weekend, speculation continues to be rife that the Chinese authorities will have to adjust their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in light of the deterioration in their competitive position over the past 12 months," said Michael Lewis, international economist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in London. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, and supported the yuan again on Monday, dealers said. The slide of the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has put Chinese exports at a competitive disadvantage. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese officials embarked on another round of comments about the yen's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda said recent moves in the yen are unfavourable for Japan as well as for Asia and the world economy. \par \par \uc2  The extent of capital outflows out of Japan was highlighted by figures released on Monday showing net foreign bond buying by Japanese investors rose sharply in July compared with June to 1.23 trillion yen after net purchases of 507.5 billion. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stuck to tight trading range around 1.78 marks. Pan-German inflation rose 0.9 percent year-on-year in July, the lowest since records began in 1991, and was up 0.3 percent on the month. \par \par \uc2  ((Astrid Zweynert London newsroom + 44 171 542 7792 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8a02u0p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
