\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Slightly Up Vs Yen On Japanese Bank Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 02:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Interbank players bought the dollar against the yen in a bid to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward a test of a new 8-year high, leaving it higher in early Tokyo trading Monday compared with its levels late in New York Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is also higher against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  "There's a feeling in the market that we have to test the 8-year high, just to get it out of our system," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Underpinning dollar bullish sentiment are ongoing worries that China may devalue the yuan - a scenario which would pulverize Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as capital takes flight for the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Market players will likely try to test Y146.73, the intraday high hit June 16. That was the dollar's highest level since Aug. 24, 1990, when it touched Y146.75. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's move upwards will be characterized by nervousness and caution over the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar's upside is seen limited to Y147.10-Y147.20, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "With the dollar near its 8-year high, people are really worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a Japanese city. \par \par \uc2  Heightening that concern, Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the International Bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reiterated warnings Monday that Japan has strong concerns about the yen's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the rise of the dollar above Y146.00, Kuroda told a small group of reporters "I'm very concerned." \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements could be exaggerated because markets have been thinned by the beginning of Japan's summer "Obon" holiday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT (8:30 P.M. EDT), the dollar is trading at Y146.30, down from Y146.39 around 0001 GMT but above Y146.27 in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at Y145.16 late in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DEM1.7805, lower than DEM1.7814 earlier but above DEM1.7802 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7746 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 10-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0040GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8a06qjg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
