\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  View: Dollar Expected To Continue Moving Upward \b0\par\par\uc2  By Marianne Sullivan \par \uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 00:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Barring dramatic developments on the Japanese economic front and short of further declines in U.S. stocks, the dollar should move higher against the yen and Deutsche mark and other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Friday's aggressive market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Canada in support of the Canadian dollar is seen by some economists as a signal the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may finally be ready to raise its benchmark rate, currently set at 5.00%, or 1/2 percentage point less than the comparable U.S. rate. \par \par \uc2  The lower yield on Canadian dollar-denominated assets is one reason Canada's dollar has continued to fall. It has also been hit by low commodity prices. \par \par \uc2  Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did succeed in lifting the CAD off its lows. Analysts suggested that the larger size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is perhaps an indication that the bank is serious about stemming the further slide of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, the U.S. dollar seemed to take its cue from the U.S. stock market, whose Dow Jones Industrial Average plunged more than 299 points Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But the market steadied late in the week, and the decline now appears "a healthy correction and not a spiral out of control that will pressure the dollar any further," said Henry Willmore, senior economist at Barclay's Capital in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar should gain additional upward momentum from U.S. economic data, which is expected to further underline the strength of the U.S. economy. The most important of this data, economists said, are July retail sales data on Thursday, expected to show a strong household sector moving into the third quarter of the year. \par \par \uc2  Capping the dollar's rise is the ever-lingering fear of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the dollar's rise above Y147.00, analysts said. "Beyond that," said Willmore of the Y147.00 level, "the market gets scared the BOJ may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 09-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2200GMT \par \par \uc2  1141 4137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8906qha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
