\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr down in Tokyo on Wall St,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  concern. \b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1998\par 05:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0300 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     143.98/00\tab \tab    144.86-143.38\par  USD/DEM     1.7685/87\tab \tab    1.7709-1.7655\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The dollar was down against the \par \par \uc2  yen at midday in Tokyo on Wednesday, as the greenback came \par \par \uc2  under pressure after an overnight tumble in New York stocks and \par \par \uc2  concerns over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the dollar pared earlier losses on bargain-hunting by \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutional investors, including some life insurers, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Concerns over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were reignited after Tuesday's comments by (Finance Minister Kiichi) Miyazawa," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa on Tuesday clarified his remarks made last week on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying he never intended to indicate that he was ruling out market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "My statements may have been insufficient or sent the wrong message," Miyazawa said on Tuesday. "It was not my intention to say that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unnecessary." \par \par \uc2  In a news conference on Friday, Miyazawa had said that yen and stock prices should basically be left to the markets. \par \par \uc2  Those comments, interpreted by markets as essentially ruling out an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen, triggered yen selling that pushed the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to a fresh seven-week low of 146.05 yen to the dollar early on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Overseas operators are now liquidating dollar longs as they have become nervous about the possibility of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  simultaneously with (Prime Minister Keizo) Obuchi's policy speech on Friday," said the trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  But other dealers said they doubted the United States will join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to possible negative effects such a move might have on New York stocks. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Federal Reserve Bank of New York jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars in New York on June 17. \par \par \uc2  "It may be too risky for the United States to conduct dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again when the U.S. stock market is looking so vulnerable, as such a move might trigger a fund flow out of the United States," a dealer at a city bank said. \par \par \uc2  New York's Dow Jones industrial average tumbled 299.43 points to end at 8,487.31 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar fell as speculative selling by U.S. operators and interbank players triggered stop-loss selling around 144.45/50, 144.00/10 and 143.85/90 yen. \par \par \uc2  Mark selling for yen by U.S. fund operators also indirectly weighed on the dollar/yen in early trade. \par \par \uc2  The greenback extended losses in mid-morning after reported remarks by Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Bureau. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda was quoted by Kyodo news agency as saying on Wednesday that the yen's excessive weakness had yet to be corrected. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar pared losses by late morning as bargain-hunting emerged from Japanese investors after the dollar hit a low of 143.38 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Buying of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen related to setting up of fresh investment trust funds also indirectly helped push the dollar/yen higher from lows. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's upside was capped by offers from U.S. fund operators around 144.10 yen and above, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark stood around 81.38/41 yen at midday, compared with around 81.74 yen in New York late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 144.80/90 yen and 1.7715/25 marks in New York on Tuesday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du8501mhr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
