cluding forecasts for heavy rains to hit the Pacific and reports of limited disruption to farm, mining and industrial production \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  KOHL/INTERVIEW \par \par \uc2  ST GILGEN, AUSTRIA - German Chancellor Helmut Kohl gives pre-election interview from his holiday home to RTL television. First extracts from interview around 1130. \par \par \uc2  ** Spot cover and focus \par \par \uc2  BONN - Finance Minister Theo Waigelnews conference on German government's long-term finance policy (0830). \par \par \uc2  ** Spot cover \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  U.N. INSPECTIONS CHIEF LEAVING IRAQ \par \par \uc2  BAGHDAD - Chief U.N. weapons inspector Richard Butler is cutting short his visit to Baghdad after encountering serious difficulties in talks with Iraqi leaders. \par \par \uc2  ** Updated focus \par \par \uc2  ** Oil markets reaction \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  If you have any queries, please call: \par \par \uc2  Singapore (65) 870-3815 \par \par \uc2  Comments to: asia.newseds@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du8400swg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
