\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Dn; Pft-Taking Spurred By MOF Talk \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1998\par 07:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--After trading above Y146.00 in the early Australasian markets, the dollar fell over one-and-a-half yen in Tokyo Tuesday as profit-taking sentiment was fueled by threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar is lower against both the yen and the Deutsche mark from its levels late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  U.S. speculators had begun selling the dollar when two senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials gave the market ample reason to book profits following the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise of more than four yen over the past several sessions. \par \par \uc2  Comments from Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the ministry's International Bureau, that Japan was prepared to take action against the "excessively weak" yen, were followed by warnings from Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa that yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be needed if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves are disruptive. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa's remarks continued the Ministry's efforts at damage control after Miyazawa played down the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, triggering the dollar's recent rise. Tuesday's comments helped take the dollar through support at Y145.30 to an intraday low of Y144.30. \par \par \uc2  "I sent a wrong message (last week) to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because my comments regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were inadequate," Miyazawa said. "I didn't mean to say that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unnecessary." \par \par \uc2  While the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worked at least temporarily, the dollar is likely to resume it assent against the yen, given Japan's bleak economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  "Today was a profit-taking driven market," said Tatsuya Ishii, senior sales manager and head of customer \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Banque Nationale de Paris in Tokyo. "It was just a very short term correction." \par \par \uc2  Around 0545 GMT (1:45 a.m. EDT), the dollar is quoted at Y144.75, below Y145.62 late Monday in New York and down from Y145.84 late Monday in London. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DEM1.7815, lower than DM1.7840 late Monday in New York and below DEM1.7843 in London Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 04-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0557GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 28038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8406lft\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
