\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Ex-MOF Oba: \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Misread Miyazawa  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Remarks \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1998\par 10:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has misread comments last week by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, and there is no shift in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy under the new government, a former senior Finance Ministry official said Monday. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities will continue to use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as a tool for containing highly volatile market activity," Tomomitsu Oba, president of the Japan Center for International Finance, a leading research institute, told Dow Jones. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the yen was sold sharply against the dollar after Miyazawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should only be used in extreme circumstances and that "we should rely on the markets to move on their own". These words, which contrasted sharply with the rhetoric on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the previous finance minister, Hikaru Matsunaga, were taken by market participants as a sign that Japan's new government was more tolerant of yen weakness. \par \par \uc2  However, Oba, a former vice finance minister for international affairs, said Monday: "Miyazawa probably doesn't bother with specific levels as long as they are deemed appropriate by the markets. \par \par \uc2  "He just left out the obvious that it's always in the interest of any \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out the volatility in the market. In this sense, there is no change in Japan's stance on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy." \par \par \uc2  Oba said two other principles also remained valid, namely that coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always more effective than stand-alone action, and that there needs to be consistent economic policy to supplement \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On prospects for future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the dollar climbs against the yen, Oba merely said the U.S. still has expectations for Japan to take action to strengthen its economy - something that was among the conditions for the U.S. agreeing to joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 17. \par \par \uc2  -By Chikako Mogi; (813) 5255-2929; cmogi@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0814GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8306h9n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
