\par\par \b \uc2  August - risky time for  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market volatility. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrew Priest \par \uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 15:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 31 (Reuters) - August is traditionally a quiet month for Western \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders swap their screens for suncream, but analysts here said on Friday a drop in volumes could increase the risk of violent price swings. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen looked particularly vulnerable to erratic price changes if lower volumes combined with the ongoing uncertainty over the Japanese government's approach to economic and fiscal reform, they said. \par \par \uc2  Thin volumes could also make \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more likely as banking authorities might be tempted to act in the hope of catching the market unawares, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "A quiet summer will make volatility in the spot market even worse," said Tony Norfield, head of treasury research at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  "Lower liquidity means the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market can be easily displaced by big orders...we've seen this over the last few weeks, dollar/yen has been whippy and erratic," he said. \par \par \uc2  Paul Chertkow, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London, said low liquidity could be the catalyst for the dollar/yen to break out from its current trading range. \par \par \uc2  "August could be a particularly volatile month and ... there is a significant risk that we could break one way or another because of the reduced liquidity," he said. \par \par \uc2  Chertkow said low liquidity would also favour \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks as prices could be moved further if volumes were low. \par \par \uc2  "Back in August 1995, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on two occasions (jointly with other central banks), so conditions of less liquidity suit both aggressive funds and worried central banks," he said. \par \par \uc2  But Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London, said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have less effect in a thin market as there was a lack of counterparties a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could trade with. \par \par \uc2  "If there's not much action going on and there is a risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most traders will just wind down positions and (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) won't sting the market very much," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said previous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions on dollar/yen had shown their success was less to do with the relative size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  compared with underlying volume than the mere presence of the banking authorities in the market. \par \par \uc2  The New York Fed said on Thursday the U.S. monetary authorities had sold a total of $833 million on June 17 when U.S. and Japanese banking authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push dollar/yen around seven yen lower. \par \par \uc2  "The best time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is when the market is on your side and you can just increase the momentum," said Barrow. "It's not the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that matters it is more down to tactics and timing." \par \par \uc2  Although a search for volume data on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is hampered by banks' unwillingness to reveal market shares, analysts said lower activity from corporate treasurers, in particular, had a big effect in reducing trading flows during the holiday period. \par \par \uc2  They said volumes in dollar/yen were further depressed because Japanese banks were hamstrung by the extra costs involved in securing euro-interbank funding - the so-called Japan premium. \par \par \uc2  Japanese banks have to pay up to 40 basis points more for interbank funds, analysts said, due to concern over the effect of a massive overhang of problem loans on the soundness of the country's banking system. \par \par \uc2  Chris Furness, senior market strategist at 4CAST, said \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows were depressed when there was a lack of reliable pointers to the future direction of economic or political policy. \par \par \uc2  "Lack of liquidity is a function of markets being pushed backwards and forwards by rumour and counterrumour," he said. \par \par \uc2  "In turn, illiquid markets mean people get worried about the prices they are making and the positions they are holding and in such instances volatility in the spot market goes up," Furness said. \par \par \uc2  Barrow said lower \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows were a symptom of a thinner western economic and political calender during July and August. \par \par \uc2  "As an economist, I'd like to think volatility depends on what is going on rather than an absence of players," he said. \par \par \uc2  "But the economic calender is designed to be quieter when there are less people around, so the effect is the same," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((London newsroom +44 171 542 6284)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du7v01cao\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
