\par\par \b \uc2  OPTIONS - Short-dated yen puts in demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 23:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, July 31 (Reuters) - Short-dated yen puts in dollar/yen options saw a second day of good demand Friday after comments from Japanese officials sent the dollar racing higher on Thursday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "More and more people are bidding to buy yen puts in short dates," said Masao Okada, chief dealer for Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank. \par \par \uc2  The demand pushed the yen put skew on risk reversals for one-month 25-delta options out to 0.35/0.45 from 0.1/0.3 the day before. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the dollar leaped after Japan's new finance minister Kiichi Miyazawa said the market should be allowed to discover the value of the yen and stocks, although \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was appropriate in "extreme cases" such as the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 -U.S. joint yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market was perfectly taken by surprise yesterday," Okada said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa sought to mitigate the damage Friday, saying the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which had been losing steam in recent days before Miyazawa's comments, shot through 143 yen on Thursday and another key level at 144.50 today. It stood at 144.65 yen Friday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's sudden revival brought the June 16 high of 146.75 yen back into focus, and a breach of that level could force more traders to rethink short-term dollar-bearish strategies, Okada said. \par \par \uc2  Short-dated risk reversals favoured yen calls when the dollar hit a peak just below 144.50 yen on July 13, he noted. \par \par \uc2  "It seems people are less afraid of the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from here," Okada said. \par \par \uc2  He predicted dollar/yen volatilities, which swelled on Thursday, would remain firm near-term following the dollar's hectic movements this week. \par \par \uc2  Weekend time decay trimmed most dollar/pair volatility levels today, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/yen slipped back to 14.9/15.1 percent from as high as 15.4/15.7 percent Thursday, and the one-year shed about 0.4 percentage point to 16.05/16.15 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark volatility collapsed to 7.5/7.8 percent in the one-month from 8.25/8.4 percent the day before as spot returned to its familiar range above 1.77 marks. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody's so fixated on Asia, there's just no interest in dollar/mark right now," said an options dealer for a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  ((Susan Kelly, Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750 chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du7v00xub\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
