\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr solid in Tokyo despite clarified  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  remarks. \b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 09:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0635 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     143.60/70\tab \tab 143.87-143.45\par  USD/DEM     1.7782/87\tab \tab 1.7821-1.7790\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, July 31 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady against \par \par \uc2  the yen in late trade on Friday despite reports that new \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa clarified his remarks on \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight that boosted the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda also \par \par \uc2  said Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance was unchanged, but these remarks were \par \par \uc2  not enough to erase the dollar's bullish tone, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Kyodo news agency quoted Miyazawa as telling reporters on Friday at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 : "All I expressed was a commonsense view. It is obvious that we will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when necessary." \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa earlier said he basically believed in leaving the yen and stock prices to the markets, which touched off strong dollar buying overseas. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly dipped on Miyazawa's comments in morning trade, but the impact was short-lived due to poor economic data including worsening jobs data and lingering speculation that there might be a subtle shift in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Traders in Tokyo were mixed about the implications of overnight remarks by Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  "Although he (Miyazawa) apparently tried to erase the impact of his overnight comments in the morning, what he said overnight could be a real intention," said a bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at a Japanese bank said, however, there will be no major shift in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "It was only a figure of speech, and that does not necessarily mean that Japan can tolerate a weakening yen," he added. A weak yen could put downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economies of Asian nations. \par \par \uc2  MOF's Kuroda said: "An excessively weak yen is undesirable for Japan, Asia, the world". \par \par \uc2  Some traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be finding it difficult to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market now amid a lack of supportive factors or positive signs for Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Japan's jobless rate jumped to a record 4.3 percent in June from 4.1 percent in May. \par \par \uc2  The jobs-to-applicants ratio fell to 0.51 in June from 0.53 in May, the lowest level since January 1978, when the government began compiling the data. \par \par \uc2  New Economic Planning Agency Minister Taichi Sakaiya told a news conference early on Friday that it is impossible to achieve the government target for growth in Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) of 1.9 percent for fiscal 1998/99. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, traders are awaiting the release of U.S. gross domestic product (GDP) data for the second quarter due out at 1230 GMT and Chicago purchasing managers' index (PMI) data for July at 1400 GMT for clues to near-term direction. \par \par \uc2  "The market expects a weak GDP figure because of the impact of the GM strike. But if the figure is strong, the dollar will be boosted in New York," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Traders said forecasts for the second-quarter GDP ranged from a 0.5 percent fall to a 1.0 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  Bids by interbank traders who had missed out on chances to buy dollars cheaply overnight and buying interest by overseas funds gave dollar support at 143.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Although sales by Japanese exporters and investors capped the dollar's rise in Tokyo, there's chance of the dollar rising to 144 yen overseas later in the day," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended 143.68/73 yen and 1.7815/25 marks in New York on Thursday. ((Tatsuo Ito/Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du7v0353f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
