\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar rise tapers off in mid-morning Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 04:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, July 31 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0151 GMT --*Dollar's rise against yen tapered off by \par \par \uc2  mid-morning Tokyo on Friday, after hitting high of 143.85 yen \par \par \uc2  after Japan's record-high unemployment rate. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar's upside capped by exporter sales, sales aimed at \par \par \uc2  protecting options with strike price at 144 yen, profit-taking \par \par \uc2  by U.S. operators. \par \par \uc2      *But dollar well-supported by month-end commercial demand, \par \par \uc2  investor demand, including Japan importers. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar at 143.71/74 yen compared with 143.68/73 in late \par \par \uc2  New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  *"The dollar rose on weak jobs data, but then dealers took a wait-and-see stance," a dealer at a major city bank said. \par \par \uc2  *Japan's unemployment rate rose to record 4.3 percent in June from 4.1 percent in May. Jobs-to-applicants ratio fell to 0.51 in June from 0.53 in May, lowest since January 1978. \par \par \uc2  *Some concerns over Japan banking system after Thomson BankWatch downgraded Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi  and Industrial Bank of Japan . \par \par \uc2  *Dollar may be pressured by sales from some Japanese trust banks liquidate some dollar-long positions and fall near low 143 yen range. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar lower against yen on media report Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa saying his overnight comments related to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were only "general principles" and he will not comment on every single \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  move. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar at 143.50/60 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar had risen sharply against yen overnight in New York after Miyazawa told news conference early on Friday he basically believes in leaving yen and stock prices to markets. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers keeping eye on U.S. second-quarter gross domestic product data at 1230 GMT. *But market already factored in weak GDP data, dealer at foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  0003 GMT - \par \par \uc2  *Dollar steady against yen in early Tokyo trade, retaining solid tone after concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  receded on overnight comments by Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar supported by month-end commercial demand and buying related to setting up of fresh trust funds. \par \par \uc2  *Profit-taking and Japanese exporter offers likely to slow pace of dollar rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *"Exporters are likely to see 143 yen as good level to sell dollars before the holiday break (in mid-August)," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said market would be watching for any comments from Finance Ministry officials that might clarify overnight comments by Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  *Miyazawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was appropriate in "extreme cases", such as recent \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 -U.S. joint yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *"People want to see if there is going to be a shift in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said a dealer at a trust bank. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du7v0301w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
