\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Minutes -2: Worried Easing Could Reignite Yen's Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 07:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan can't ignore the effect that an easing in its monetary policy would have on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, particularly when the yen's weakness is a common concern among Asian nations, according to the minutes of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making board meeting released Friday, \par \par \uc2  The minutes of the June 25 meeting said that the members regarded a further monetary easing as inappropriate in the wake of a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the yen on June 17. \par \par \uc2  "At this time, so soon after the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is unsuitable to take a monetary policy which could reignite the yen's weakness," the minutes said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 31-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0526GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7v06iyy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
