\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  dealers reserve Obuchi judgement, eye charts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Astrid Zweynert \par \uc2 861 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1998\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 28 (Reuters) - It's crunchtime for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to make up its mind about the new face of Japanese politics, and chart watchers said on Tuesday a key technical formation may provide the first clue. \par \par \uc2  While the yen may look stable, having traded in narrow ranges for much of the past week, technical analysts on Tuesday said this hiatus was likely to end soon. \par \par \uc2  A triangle pattern has been forming over the past six weeks, and dollar/yen is sandwiched between its top line around 142.65-143.10 yen and a support line that cuts in just below 140. At the moment the pressure is on the dollar's upside. \par \par \uc2  "We're watching 142.65 closely because if the dollar is breaking higher through the triangle top we could see the 146.75 high again," said Ian Stannard, technical analyst at Chase. \par \par \uc2  The triangle pattern began with the dollar's near eight-year high of 146.75 yen, set on June 19. That was right before an unexpected burst of U.S.-led \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sent the dollar down more than 13 yen to 133.60, where the bottom of the triangle begins. \par \par \uc2  Since then, that range has steadily narrowed and is now down to a few yen. At 1130 GMT the yen was at 141.90/142.00 per dollar, compared with 142.30/40 in late Europe on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The swings back and forth within this constricting pattern have been largely dictated by the unfolding political saga. \par \par \uc2  Prime minister-designate Keizo Obuchi was pressing ahead on Tuesday with his search to fill key cabinet posts amid signs that LDP elder Kiichi Miyazawa might become finance minister. \par \par \uc2  Yen sentiment had improved after former Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto resigned after a crushing defeat for his ruling Liberal Democrat Party (LDP) in Upper House elections on July 12. \par \par \uc2  The yen strengthened to 138.53 per dollar on July 20 from around 142 prior to the election. \par \par \uc2  Since then it has suffered a setback, falling to a low of 142.69 on Tuesday amid market scepticism that Obuchi's new team would make quick progress in implementing measures to kickstart the ailing Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  Obuchi said on Tuesday it was unlikely parliament would immediately decide a fundamental overhaul of Japan's tax system. \par \par \uc2  If the dollar does break to the upside, a move to the 146.75 is bound to get people talking about 150 yen again. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think a break-out is imminent but we have not abandoned our 'dollar/yen at 150' scenario," said Nick Parsons, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas in London. "There is not much point in buying yen unless you get clear signals of an economic recovery in Japan." \par \par \uc2  Against the mark, the yen is still entrenched in a downtrend even though it bounced back from a near-six week low around 80 yen to around 79.30 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "A break through 143.10 and 80 (against the mark) would be the catalyst for a new leg of yen weakness," said Parsons. \par \par \uc2  Stannard at Chase said the area around 80 coincides with a longterm trendline and the top end of a descending channel from the mark's high in 1990 at 96.25. \par \par \uc2  Above 80, the major target is the 1998 high from June 16 at 80.92. The 79.30/20 area is now key support, representing a former triangle top which the mark eroded last Friday. \par \par \uc2  "If we can hold here than the signs are that 80 will be broken and then we're off to the 80.90/95 June highs," said Stannard. Medium-term there was scope to 82.40. \par \par \uc2  The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might make dollar/yen gains choppy though, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But so long as dollar gains are slow and Asian markets remain stable, a fresh bout of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked less likely at this stage, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If yen losses are gradual then \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is less likely than it would be if we had sudden sharp movements," said Michael Metcalfe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at NatWest Markets. \par \par \uc2  Rumours that the Federal Reserve had sold Treasury bills for a customer on Thursday fueled speculation about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as dealers said the BOJ may have been the customer that needed liquidity for future yen purchases. \par \par \uc2  When the U.S. rode to the yen's support in June, U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said it had provided "a window of opportunity" for Japan to address its economic and financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite unlikely the Fed will step in again at this stage," said Parsons. "The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June was done to spur \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  into action but now the U.S. is likely to want to see some action first before helping Japan again." \par \par \uc2  However, as the Fed and the BOJ caught the markets by surprise with their dollar-selling spree in June, caution might be the safest bet. \par \par \uc2  ((London newsroom + 44 171 542 7792 fax +44 171 542 5293, \par \par \uc2  uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010924du7s01dts\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
