\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar up vs yen on Moody's action, but off high. \b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1998\par 08:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0635 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     141.75/80\tab \tab 142.10-140.10\par  USD/DEM     1.7903/06\tab \tab 1.7931-1.7880\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, July 23 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against \par \par \uc2  the yen in late Thursday trade as the yen suffered from action \par \par \uc2  by Moody's Investor Service that put Japan's country debt \par \par \uc2  rating under review for a possible downgrade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback came off earlier highs by late trade due \par \par \uc2  to fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ahead of Friday's \par \par \uc2  vote for leader of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party. \par \par \uc2  Moody's said it had placed on review for possible downgrade Japan's Aaa country ceilings for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated debt and bank deposits as well as the Aaa-rated yen-denominated securities issued or guaranteed by the government of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The dollar shot up to as high as 142.10 yen but then slashed gains due to profit-taking and exporter sales. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's abrupt rise reminded traders of the risk the BOJ might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it did in April, when Moody's announced it had changed the outlook of the Japanese government debt rating to negative. "Worry about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and limited falls in stocks capped the dollar's gains," said one bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of the International Bureau at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Thursday that there was no need to comment on Moody's action. \par \par \uc2  Traders in Tokyo were mixed about the dollar's further rise but some said the yen may lose ground further overseas in a reaction to Moody's action. Ko Haruki, manager and chief dealer of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at HSBC Midland said the dollar is likely to rise 145 yen within a week, after Moody's action. \par \par \uc2  "Until the Japanese government forms a new cabinet, which will take about a week, it may be difficult for the monetary authorities to prop up the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government came under more pressure over the Moody's action just a day before the ruling LDP's presidential race on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "(Moody's announcement) will renew interest in the LDP presidential race, as it will put more pressure on Japan's new government to take action," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Keizo Obuchi, the establishment candidate of the the ruling Liberal Democratic Party, appeared to be closing in on the post of LDP president. Health Minister Junichiro Koizumi and veteran politician Seiroku Kajiyama are also vying to replace Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto. \par \par \uc2  Hashimoto is resigning over the LDP's poor showing in elections for the Upper House of parliament on July 12. \par \par \uc2  Kajiyama said on Thursday he wants to establish a basis for the nation to pull itself out of recession within a year. \par \par \uc2  Traders think the yen could rise briefly if Kajiyama is elected. But the focus is shifting to how swiftly whoever is new prime minister can implement his economic policies. \par \par \uc2  An extraordinary session of parliament to nominate the prime minister and approve much-anticipated bills to address Japan banks' bad loans is expected to be held at the end of this month or early August. \par \par \uc2  The action by Moody's is a message to Japan's next government to act fast on economic policy and the banking system's bad loan problems, Yasuhisa Shiozaki, parliamentary vice finance minister, said on Thursday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said recent weakness in the stock market supported dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  Shuji Kawanabe, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at JP Morgan in Tokyo, said the failure to sustain a recent rally in the stock market could make domestic investors less eager to invest there and instead prompt them to invest aboard. \par \par \uc2  The linkage between the dollar/yen rate and the Nikkei stock average strengthened recently as overseas operators see stock prices as a barometer of Japan's economic health, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei 225 average fell 105.05 points or 0.64 percent to end at 16,188.01. The average briefly fell as low as 16,158.44. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 141.18/21 yen and 1.7883/86 marks in New York on Wednesday. ((Tatsuo Ito, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7n009i1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
