\par\par \b \uc2  =Dlr/Yen Volatility -2:Million Bucks Riding On Options Play \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1998\par 18:01\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Since June of last year, implied volatility in\par dollar/yen has averaged between 8%-10% - and those are\par typical levels, said Eric Nickerson, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at\par Bank of America in New York.\par    Only recently have levels hugged 20% as the dollar has\par gyrated dramatically - between highs around Y146 and lows\par around Y133 just last month. Mary Beth Slack, senior options\par analyst with Technical Data in New York, pointed out that\par implied volatility in dollar/yen rose from around 12% June 9\par to around 18% by June 19.\par    "In the long run volatilities are at the high end of\par their range, but that is justifiable given the range in the\par spot market," said one options dealer in New York.\par    Indeed, with unpredictable swings in the dollar against\par the yen - stemming from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , knee-jerk\par reaction to the latest talk on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tax policy and now a\par leaderless nation - options traders say they are finding it\par hard to sell volatility, a move that bets on a tame\par dollar/yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    They can't buy volatility either because it's expensive.\par Premium, or an options' cost, rises as volatility rises.\par This leaves some options traders looking at so-called\par "double no-touch" options that try to take advantage of the\par high volatility levels and capture the dollar/yen range - at\par an affordable cost, said Technical Data's Slack.\par    Some of the bigger options volatility plays seen Tuesday\par involved the purchase of Y125-Y155 options strikes worth $1\par million when it expires in four months time. In the double\par no-touch option, if the dollar doesn't hit either Y125 or\par Y155 by the time the option expires, the options buyer reaps\par in $1 million, said Masao Okada, vice president and chief\par options trader at Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank in New York.\par    Such an option is cheap relative to buying outright\par volatility because the option automatically becomes\par worthless if the dollar touches either strike anytime before\par the option's expiration, Okada explained.\par    -By J.R. Wu; 201-938-4384\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  07-15-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1201EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4215 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du7f01pcn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
