\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Russia, IMF Agreement Supports DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1998\par 03:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at Y78.81, down from Y79.12 earlier but above Y77.66 in New York late Friday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Friday at Y77.32. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6320, up from $1.6290 earlier and below $1.6330 in New York late Friday. Sterling was at $1.6305 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  While Japan comes to grips with forming a new government, market players are concerned policy vacuum, with some saying the lack of clear leadership in Tokyo could dissuade the U.S. from joining in coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials sought to put to rest such concerns, with Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the finance bureau, saying that the Group of Seven agreement to promote \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability remains in place. \par \par \uc2  But traders said such doubts persist. \par \par \uc2  "Until the changes are made, there will be blank periods, and people are concerned about those blank periods," said Tatsuya Ishii, senior sales manager and head of customer \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Banque Nationale de Paris in Tokyo. But Ishii and other dealers said they don't expect any major policy shifts by Japan. \par \par \uc2  There is concern, however, that without control over the upper house, the LDP will need the cooperation of other parties to pass key legislation, particularly key legislation related to the bridge bank scheme to help stabilize the financial system. \par \par \uc2  "There was a lot of resistance to the bridge bank plan among opposition politicians," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in trading, the mark is finding support from an agreement between Russia and the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  The two sides Sunday reached an agreement on all the key issues of a loan package to bailout the sinking Russian economy, the Interfax news agency said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is quoted at 6.1011 French francs, up from FF6.0915 late Friday in New York, following France's victory in the World Cup over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  "Our colleagues in France are all bringing champagne to work," said a Tokyo-based dealer at a French bank. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar is seen trading between Y142.50-Y145.00 for the rest of the\par Asian session Monday, traders said.\par By Arran Scott, 813-5255-2984; amscott@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0107GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7d05w5x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
