\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Speculation About BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 1998\par 08:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said until more definitive signs emerge that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to implement permanent tax cuts, the yen probably won't get much more of a boost against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We're still looking at what kind of details will come up," said Yasuhisa Morikuni, assistant vice president of treasury at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Mitsubishi Trust's Kurosawa added that the manner in which such a step is announced may be as important as the tax cuts themselves in boosting the yen. "It seems like there will be permanent income tax cuts. But the impact will depend on how Japan makes the announcement," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, despite some traders' speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would time its yen-supportive action to coincide with major policy announcements by the Japanese government. \par \par \uc2  Market players had been on alert for BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday immediately after an announcement by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it formally endorsed a bridge bank plan to restructure its financial system by protecting sound borrowers from collapsed banks and putting failed banks under state control. \par \par \uc2  And again on Friday, some dealers speculated that the BOJ may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Hashimoto's remarks. They reasoned that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inspired dollar falls would be accelerated because of thin trading conditions, with the New York market closed for holiday on Friday. However, there has been no sign of BOJ action so far Friday, according to Tokyo traders. \par \par \uc2  Opinion is divided on whether the BOJ will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon. Morikuni said the BOJ probably won't enter the market at a time when market players are already bracing themselves for such action. "I don't think the possibility (of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday) is very high," he said. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at Y76.81, down from Y77.45 in New York Thursday and below Y77.81 in London Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6590, down from $1.6593 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.6570 in London late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0649GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7305mn9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
