\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ June dlr sales estimated at $1.04 bln-bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1998\par 06:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 1 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) sold an estimated $1.04 billion to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in June, bankers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  BOJ data showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) received 145.8 billion yen from the private sector in June through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say MOF's receipts from the private sector less its sales of financing bills (FBs) roughly represent the amount of dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yen terms. \par \par \uc2  MOF conducted no FB sales to the private sector in June. \par \par \uc2  The private sector includes commercial banks, foreign central banks, municipal governments, public funds and quasi-governmental institutions. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ confirmed it had acted jointly with the Federal Reserve Bank of New York to sell dollars on June 17 in New York. \par \par \uc2  Some bankers believe the BOJ may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone in Tokyo trade on June 17. \par \par \uc2  The data released by the BOJ suggests the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June was much smaller than estimates heard previously in the market. \par \par \uc2  The market had previously estimated that the BOJ spent at least $4 billion and the New York Fed $2 billion in coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that day. \par \par \uc2  However, some traders believe the New York Fed sold only a few hundred million dollars for yen with the BOJ on June 17 in New York. The dollar moved in a range from 144.10 yen to 136 that day in New York and Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo trade during the month, the dollar hit a high of 146.75 yen on June 16, and a low of 134.50 yen on June 19. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7101qq9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
