\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Foreign Reserves -2: Follows May's $1.22 Bln Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 165 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1998\par 09:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's reserves of convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights decreased by $1.10 billion in June from the preceding month to $205.87 billion, the Finance Ministry said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The decline followed May's rise of $1.22 billion from April. A large decline in the value of reserves was expected for June in light of the yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets carried out by the Bank of Japan and the U.S. Federal Reserve on June 17. \par \par \uc2  Traders had estimated the BOJ and Fed spent a combined $3.0 billion-$4.0 billion in propping up the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  providing the bulk of the funds. \par \par \uc2  Normally, in months without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves increase by between $1.0 billion and $2.0 billion due to interest earned on holdings. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 01-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0739GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7105mpp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
