\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr ends quiet U.S. mixed, Russia pressures mark. \b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1998\par 22:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 29 (Reuters) - The dollar ended mixed in quiet trade, with the mark losing support amid speculation that Germany's large investments in Russia were being jeopardised by Moscow's mounting financial crisis, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Activity was extremely light ahead of a two-day meeting of Federal Reserve policy makers on Tuesday and Wednesday, the widely watched monthly U.S. employment report on Thursday and the Fourth of July long weekend starting Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is just digesting everything. It's going to get ready to have a big move in the next couple of days," said Russell LaScala, chief dealer at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped to 141.65/75 yen, from 141.73/83 at the open. It rose to 1.8105/15 marks from 1.8080/90. \par \par \uc2  The mark weakened against the yen and pound after the World Bank said the Russian government had asked it to speed up payment of a $500-to-$600 million loan due in October, to help Moscow make up worrisome budget shortfalls. \par \par \uc2  Investor confidence in Russia's ability to cover its deficits, and retain enough \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to avert a devaluation of the rouble, has been evaporating rapidly in recent days. \par \par \uc2  Fears about Russia's ability to meet debt payments resurfaced last week, even though the International Monetary Fund okayed the release of a delayed $670 million payment. \par \par \uc2  Germany, one of Russia's largest lenders, is seen most at risk if the country defaults on its international obligations. \par \par \uc2  The market is looking for the IMF to grant $10-$15 billion in new emergency loans. But the agency is only willing to let go of that money if Russia undertakes real economic reform. \par \par \uc2  Russia's benchmark RTS share index closed down 6.11 percent and yields on Russian Treasury securities rose again on Monday, after soaring to around 70 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps pushing up interest rates, finding it increasingly difficult to attract the foreign capital it needs to cover its short-term cash flow needs. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the dollar rose to 143.35 yen, its highest level since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets nearly two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  The dollar erased those early gains after the Bank of Japan released its quarterly tankan report of business confidence, which showed that sentiment, while gloomy, was better than expected. The diffusion index came in at minus 38, versus forecasts of -42 or worse and the March tankan, which was -31. \par \par \uc2  Yen trading was focused on Thursday's expected release of the outline of Japan's bridge bank plan to take over the assets of failed financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen remained in a tight range. Lingering fears of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  discouraged buying, but the dollar was mostly supported above 141.50 by ongoing alarm about Japan's distressed economy. \par \par \uc2  "The strength of the dollar against the yen is also helping to hold up the dollar-mark," said a trader at a German bank. "U.S. stocks have been going really strong the last week and that's helping it as well." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the pound slipped a hair to $1.6660/70 from $1.6665/75 at the open. The dollar inched up to 1.5225/35 Swiss from 1.5220/30 and to Canadian $1.4702/07 from C$1.4698/03. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar closed at $0.6070/75, up from $0.6055/65. \par \par \uc2  ((-Alden Bentley, 212 859 1667)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6t01ua7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
