\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup:Dlr Drops, Recovers Post Tankan Selling \b0\par\par\uc2  By James Simms \par \uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1998\par 08:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar is slightly higher against the yen Monday compared to New York levels Friday after a swing of nearly two yen before and after the release of the closely watched Bank of Japan "tankan" survey of corporate sentiment. It is also barely up against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  After rising to Y143.30 early - its highest level since the June 17 U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - on buying by Japanese investment trusts ahead of the release of the tankan data, the dollar fell against the yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly survey was slightly less dismal than expected. \par \par \uc2  The tankan's diffusion index (DI) for big manufacturers, measuring the percentage of companies who think conditions are improving minus those who see them deteriorating, came in at minus 38, a tad better than the minus 44 forecast on average by economists surveyed by Dow Jones. The previous survey, in March, showed a DI reading of minus 31. \par \par \uc2  Having bought the dollar on the rumor of a poor tankan, U.S. hedge funds sold on the fact, booking profits and pushing the dollar to an intraday low of Y141.45 at 0228 GMT (10:28 p.m. Subday EDT), before Japanese trusts and hedge funds pushed the dollar back up against the yen in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. funds' sales were in good amounts," said Shuji Takano, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ABN-Amro in Tokyo, adding that overseas players had carried long-dollar positions since last week and used the opportunity to unwind them. \par \par \uc2  Shizuo Nakamura, corporate dealer at Barclays Bank, added that foreign funds increasing their asset allocation in Nikkei stock futures prompted yen buying earlier. \par \par \uc2  Around 0555 GMT (1:55 a.m. EDT), the dollar is quoted at Y142.05, just above Y141.98 late Friday in New York but down from Y142.85 late Friday in London. It also is at DEM1.8110, barely higher than DEM1.8100 late Friday in New York but below DEM1.8125 in London Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 29-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0613GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6t05i3f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
